  [38;5;153merrors[39m contains only failing fields, and [38;5;153mvalid[39m is exactly [38;5;153mObject.keys(errors).length === 0[39m. The first failing rule for
  a field wins; remaining rules for that field are skipped. This replaces today's single [38;5;153merror[39m string, which can't
  represent two bad fields at once.

  [1mEdge cases, decided explicitly[0m (these are the things that cause bugs when left implicit):

  - [1mWhat counts as empty for [38;5;153mrequired()[39m:[0m [38;5;153mundefined[39m, [38;5;153mnull[39m, [38;5;153m""[39m, a whitespace-only string, an empty array, and [38;5;153mfalse[39m (an
    unchecked checkbox). Notably [38;5;153m0[39m passes — it's a real value.
  - [1mNo mutation.[0m [38;5;153mvalidate()[39m never trims or coerces the caller's values. [38;5;153mrequired()[39m ignores surrounding whitespace when
    deciding emptiness, but the value the form submits is whatever the form had.
  - [1mFields in [38;5;153mvalues[39m but not in [38;5;153mschema[39m are ignored[0m — forms often carry state that isn't user input.
  - [1mFields in [38;5;153mschema[39m but missing from [38;5;153mvalues[0m are validated as [38;5;153mundefined[39m, so [38;5;153mrequired()[39m catches them.
  - [1mType mismatches throw.[0m [38;5;153mminLength(3)[39m against a number, or a schema entry that isn't an array of functions, throws a
    [38;5;153mTypeError[39m naming the field. These are schema bugs, not user errors; failing loudly means a test catches them instead
    of a form silently accepting anything.

  [1mMigration of the login form:[0m [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m is deleted from [38;5;153mapp.js[39m and replaced by a [38;5;153mloginSchema[39m const plus a [38;5;153mvalidate()
[39m  call. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m's script tag becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, which is what requires serving over HTTP
  rather than [38;5;153mfile://[39m.

  [1mOne thing I want to flag rather than decide for you:[0m [38;5;153mapp.js[39m today only [38;5;153mconsole.error[39ms validation failures — nothing is
  ever shown to the user. Keeping the shared layer validator-only (your Section-1 choice) means error [3mdisplay[0m is each
  form's own job, and the login form currently has no display. I can leave that as-is, or add error rendering to the
  login form only, as ordinary form code and not shared infrastructure.
